=== text ===
A **ternary** system is a classification system that uses three distinct, mutually exclusive, and mutually exclusive categories to classify items, rather than grouping them into just two categories (like binary classification) or a single continuous spectrum.

In the context of logic or logic programming, this is often referred to as a **ternary logic** system, where the truth value of a proposition can be one of three states: **True**, **false**, or an **unknown/unknown**
